cff-version: 1.2.0
title: whybox
message: >-
  This project is a scaffold for the science sandboxes framework. If you use
  it, please cite the paper that introduced the framework, below.
type: software
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A toolkit for building, running, and grading science sandboxes: closed
  experimental settings in which an investigator submits specimens to a sealed
  oracle, reads back a small report, and must infer the hidden rule behind it.
  Grades the score and the stated understanding separately, on the grounds that
  the two come apart.
references:
  - type: article
    title: Science sandboxes measure the scientific capability of AI agents
    year: 2026
    journal: arXiv
    notes: >-
      arXiv:2608.30165 [q-bio.QM]. The authors' own implementation is at
      https://github.com/asr2210/science-sandbox, MIT License,
      Copyright (c) 2025 Ananth Rao. This project matches that license and
      reimplements the ideas rather than their code.
